+ * A tin is a TABLE, so it cannot drift at runtime the way a formula does; it drifts AT REST,
+ * when a second hand writes a copy somewhere else and the two part company. The pass-5 cut keyed
+ * a copy on a variable's NAME and on six-digit hexes EQUAL to the sheet, and ten of fourteen
+ * fresh second publishers walked through it (a scalar, a nested neutral key, a drifted table
+ * under a neutral name, a templated `setProperty`, oklch / rgb / 3- and 8-digit literals, a CSS
+ * alias, a `.js` file). This cut keys on the COLOUR, whatever it is called and however spelled:
+ *
+ *   4a  NO SECOND PUBLISHER. Every `.css/.vue/.ts/.mts/.js/.mjs/.html` under `src/` and `e2e/`,
+ *       plus `index.html`, read with comments stripped. RED:
+ *         · a `--color-peer-N[-ring|-name]` or `--peer-*-l` DECLARED anywhere but index.css — a
+ *           rule, a quoted style key, a `setProperty`, and a TEMPLATED name (`--color-peer-${…}`)
